  "method": "Each timed arm started from a separate fresh populated Homebrew clone. The prototype asked Git to build a v4 index from the authenticated manifest in a temporary bare repository during reservation. After workspace initialization it wrote the prepared bytes into the private scratch index, synced the file and performed normal stage-zero readback and checkout attribute evaluation. Native was git worktree add. OS caches and machine activity were uncontrolled.",
  "checks": "The prototype reported that it used the early index on every default comparison. Before running status, the standard and candidate private indexes were byte-identical. Each graft shared all 3318 regular files and reported zero private working-file bytes, matched the selected commit and tree, had clean status, exposed one commit and passed strict fsck.",
